THOUGHT: The NullAway error is because `getProperty` is annotated as `@Nullable`, so `this.getProperty(propertyName).setType(type);` may dereference null. I should mirror the pattern used in `getTypeOfProperty`: store the result in a local variable, check for null, and only call `setType` if non-null. Then I’ll run the Gradle compile to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '62,66s/public void setTypeOfProperty(String propertyName, String type) {
    this.getProperty(propertyName).setType(type);
  }/public void setTypeOfProperty(String propertyName, String type) {
    ICustomProperty property = this.getProperty(propertyName);
    if (property != null) {
      property.setType(type);
    }
  }/' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/environment/tilemap/xml/CustomPropertyProvider.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "CustomPropertyProvider" -n new_build_output.log || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

